{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443270-2e-the-last-three-crowns","id":1443270,"title":"[2e] The Last Three Crowns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-09T10:01:31-07:00","id":1443270,"title":"[2e] The Last Three Crowns","content":"As the title might suggest, I've been tinkering with a separate Mage project, and as part of that I ended up formulating Crowns for the Prelacies of the Ruin, the Nemesis and the Psychopomp. I'd welcome anything anyone has to say on them:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ruin grants the </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crown of Certainty</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. She adds her Fate Praxis dots to any opposed Extended action. Additionally, she no longer tires or becomes exhausted, and once per day may gain a point of Willpower when she succeeds on an Extended action to bring ruin, desolation, hopelessness or pessimism to others.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Nemesis grants the </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crown of Innocence</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Any character attempting to trace responsibility for an action back to or perceive the bearer of the Crown, including by identifying her Signature Nimbus, suffers a penalty equal to her Spirit Praxis dots. Additionally, she is always considered to have the ability to hide or conceal herself, though she may suffer penalties in especially open or exposed environments.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Psychopomp grants the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Crown of Mortality</b>.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The character gains health levels equal to her Death Praxis dots, will not die of old age or attendant health defects (though she still ages), and does not take damage each minute if her health bear is filled with Lethal damage, though she may fall unconscious as normal.</span></span></div> <br /> <b>Note</b>: The Crowns of the Archigenitors are in Mage 2e core, while the Crowns of the Chancellor, the Raptor and the Prophet are in <i>Signs of Sorcery, </i>p. 122, for anyone looking for the rest<i><b>.</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-09-2021, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T10:20:43-07:00","id":1443275,"title":"","content":"I think this link might help, also nemesis\u2019s crown was in dark eras. Crown of secrecy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments/page5\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments/page5\"> Let's Cook Up Some Crown Attainments - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments/page5\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/892970-let-s-cook-up-some-crown-attainments/page5 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So we have Crown Attainments for Forces, Mind, Prime, and Space. Let's make some for the rest of the Arcana. Looking at the existing Crowns, the following things stand out: &bull; They are obviously themed after the Exarch in question. So Life's Crown Attainment is going to be the Crown of Predation, not the Crown of Growth. &bull; They consist of two benefits. &bull; The first benefit is roughly equivalent to a Utility Attainment, but a bit better - remove the Mana cost for something, get a new way to recover Mana, etcetera. &bull; The second benefit scales with the Arcana rating, and look like they're more </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link